  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "The earlier answer is correct and agrees with the captured solution. The determinant is 9+2\\sqrt{0.7}>0, so the coefficient matrix is invertible and the lines intersect at exactly one point. Thus I and III are true and II is false. The source loosely says uniqueness for every right-hand side was given; only uniqueness for this system was given, but for a square matrix that implies invertibility and hence uniqueness for every right-hand side.",
